# Defect 072, closed 2026-09-20 at M-declared-extents step 18, on panel 170's
# narrowing of `one_tag_one_type` at `tag void`.
#
# SYMPTOM. Two C allocator families that both hand back `void *` had no tag to
# differ by, so `one_tag_one_type` collapsed them onto ONE Heroes type and the
# crossed free became an ordinary call: `check` 0, `build` 0, `run` 0, the arena
# destroyed and the heap block leaked, and the handle live set silent because
# the count balanced — two acquired, two consumed.
#
# CAUSE, and it is the rule defeating its own ground. `one_tag_one_type` exists
# because two Heroes types over one tag would put the checker and clang on
# opposite sides and *"the mutant survives every instrument the language has"*
# (defect 029, panel 145). **At `tag void` the rule PRODUCES that shape instead
# of preventing it**: it forces one type where the author needs two, and the
# swap it exists to kill becomes legal.
#
# THE REPAIR is one condition, and it names `void` and no other word, because
# every other tag is a name the author can vary — `record Arena tag arena_t`
# beside `record Heap tag heap_t` already works where the header declares both,
# and the census that opened this found the pair only where the header declares
# neither.
#
# WHAT STAYS REFUSED, and this case's sibling asserts it:
# `tests/golden/check/` still refuses two handles over a real tag with
# `error[duplicate_tag]`. The rule is intact where it has a tag to work with.
#
# This case is the MATCHED program — each block freed by its own family's
# deallocator — because that is what the narrowing makes writable. The crossed
# program is the check-tree case beside it.

extern "fixedbugs-two-allocator-families-over-one-void.h"
    record Arena tag void
    record Heap tag void
    function arena_new() -> Arena acquires arena_free
    function arena_free(b: Arena consumes)
    function heap_new() -> Heap acquires heap_free
    function heap_free(b: Heap consumes)

function main()
    a = arena_new()
    h = heap_new()

    # Each to its own, which is the program the author meant and could not
    # write: before the narrowing these two were one type.
    arena_free(b: a)
    heap_free(b: h)
